# Generated research reports (pipeline output, not source)
research_vault/*
!research_vault/EXAMPLE_NVDA_report.md

# Panel snapshots (build artifacts — reproducible from the manifest)
data/panel/
.vercel
.env*

# ── Research data: acquired, never committed ────────────────────────────────
#
# `datasets/` holds Dolt clones measured at 14 GB (stocks 4.4G, options 8.0G,
# earnings 1.7G, rates 13M). `data/research/` holds the derived partitions,
# universe, model registry and study reports.
#
# Neither is committed, and neither needs to be: both are reproducible from
# recorded provenance. Every raw manifest records the clone's resolved COMMIT
# HASH (e.g. stocks@h4k31feneele009f7t15a022qjtn2970), not a branch name, so a
# rebuild can be pinned to the same bytes. Acquisition is documented in
# docs/research-data.md and docs/dataset-catalog.md.
#
#   dolt clone post-no-preference/stocks datasets/stocks
#   python -m scripts.quant.local_backfill --stage all
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. An unanchored `datasets/` matches a directory
# of that name at ANY depth, which silently excluded `src/quant/datasets/` —
# the entire ingestion package — from a commit. Anchored to the repository root
# it means only the clones.
/datasets/
/data/research/

# ...except the model register, which is not data.
#
# `/data/research/` exists to exclude derived partitions measured in gigabytes.
# The register is a 1.5 MB evidence ledger that records every model, its
# metrics, and its promotion state — and it is the ONLY place a promotion can be
# recorded. It was caught by this rule because of where it happens to live, and
# the consequence reached production: the deployed backend read no register,
# found no entries, and reported "no model is validated" as a conclusion drawn
# from a file that was not in the image.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file beneath an excluded directory, so the whole path
# chain is re-admitted one level at a time. The `*` lines keep everything else
# in those directories excluded.
!/data/research/
/data/research/*
!/data/research/models/
/data/research/models/*
!/data/research/models/registry.json
/data/panel/

# Training and ingestion logs — reproducible output, often large.
/logs/

# Experiment artifacts: keep the ones a decision rests on, exclude the bulk.
#
# metrics/config/manifest/folds/portfolio are small and are the evidence a
# reader needs. Per-row predictions run to tens of megabytes and are fully
# regenerable from the recorded seed, dataset content hash and git commit, so
# they stay local — the same rule that keeps raw partitions out.
experiments/*/predictions_*.parquet
